s time-limited, because\nthe group has lost its margin and the next failure defeats it.\n\n**Redundancy is a claim, not a fact.** Check whether the redundant partner is healthy before crediting\nit. If findings exist against both legs of a redundant pair in the same batch, the pair is not\nredundant. Assessing each finding in isolation misses this.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-903ab03e1efb3dc8244d8a5953d10d5ab69d5ae2b40e92b9cbd1963baef59c6f"},"item-3657959f1a17e70851f3d2e424d25edb":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-e0187bd546eaa1b96f965f47bee851ffdae7a9e9204867f23b769ffb383ba402"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":["rainbow doors","split lights"],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Prism-Gates\r\n","unit_id":"u0005"},{"quote":"Aliases: rainbow doors; split lights\r\n","unit_id":"u0006"}],"item_id":"item-3657959f1a17e70851f3d2e424d25edb","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Prism-Gates"],"source_id":"eval_prism","source_sha256":"72765663cf1ff3ff2fb8cd92bbae6051dc4f10493b1df2dfe0452865068c32c1","spans":[{"end":106,"start":90},{"end":126,"start":106},{"end":164,"start":126},{"end":224,"start":164},{"end":292,"start":224},{"end":294,"start":292}],"status":"active","text":"## Prism-Gates\r\nScope: Prism-Gates\r\nAliases: rainbow doors; split lights\r\nDo not open Prism-Gates when the violet card is face down.\r\nIf the card is face up, opening is allowed except during the hush.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-e0187bd546eaa1b96f965f47bee851ffdae7a9e9204867f23b769ffb383ba402"},"item-55a75be555f5e1bb6868359497e5f76b":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-11f54aba12f6476a5bc74541bba641b151864ca365845fafea0a4e604cf403ae"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Lemon Cubes\r\n","unit_id":"u0019"}],"item_id":"item-55a75be555f5e1bb6868359497e5f76b","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Lemon Cubes"],"source_id":"eval_orchard","source_sha256":"412ea94c07b410bb43a46c04e98de2acfcaca0d5641e39f9f6f8e035f893d66c","spans":[{"end":643,"start":616},{"end":663,"start":643},{"end":707,"start":663},{"end":751,"start":707}],"status":"active","text":"## Branch for Lemon Cubes\r\nScope: Lemon Cubes\r\nPlace Lemon Cubes on a paper coaster only.\r\nPlace Lemon Cubes on a paper coaster only.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-11f54aba12f6476a5bc74541bba641b151864ca365845fafea0a4e604cf403ae"},"item-6654ef60c3a845ce7c9ad1c042d22c70":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-5b37599057cc8e112ce21637429a4f86179ddc5d7ac4feccedf1a88c4569583a"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-6654ef60c3a845ce7c9ad1c042d22c70","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"eval_loom","source_sha256":"7c10850f21de579945f1daa3d62353b9fba505a9a78c18ea04049b6fa21c3cfc","spans":[{"end":318,"start":285},{"end":397,"start":318},{"end":472,"start":397},{"end":542,"start":472},{"end":632,"start":542},{"end":634,"start":632}],"status":"active","text":"## Entry 07: late qualification\r\n07:00 Exception: a green tassel does not permit sending during a silent beat.\r\n07:01 The silent-beat exception qualifies the earlier sending permission.\r\n07:02 Higher thread reserve means lower snag likelihood, not higher.\r\n07:03 The drum is logged clear and possibly covered; neither account resolves the other.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-5b37599057cc8e112ce21637429a4f86179ddc5d7ac4feccedf1a88c4569583a"},"item-70e3a31707646a5a657ec26cb721754b":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-3ead0128d76d4605316197d68e9ed3836c6e9b594c3b9d52e730b7dc749ae509"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Equipment: Cork Rings\r\n","unit_id":"u0017"}],"item_id":"item-70e3a31707646a5a657ec26cb721754b","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Cork Rings"],"source_id":"eval_loom","source_sha256":"7c10850f21de579945f1daa3d62353b9fba505a9a78c18ea04049b6fa21c3cfc","spans":[{"end":659,"start":634},{"end":682,"start":659},{"end":729,"start":682},{"end":776,"start":729}],"status":"active","text":"## Entry 08: Cork Rings\r\nEquipment: Cork Rings\r\n08:00 Put Cork Rings beside the marked spool.\r\n08:00 Put Cork Rings beside the marked spool.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-3ead0128d76d4605316197d68e9ed3836c6e9b594c3b9d52e730b7dc749ae509"},"item-75bfb2af1b683e4c5368b00b504b2d87":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-3981f0e8264100841775e8c781660c754bd8d8437e5a11fe72c209d41ae09edb"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-75bfb2af1b683e4c5368b00b504b2d87","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"eval_river","source_sha256":"cb87dd0ce116a2813451daa873830d5b53269ac41742330b6d4baee09b61663e","spans":[{"end":42,"start":0},{"end":125,"start":42},{"end":193,"start":125},{"end":258,"start":193},{"end":353,"start":258},{"end":425,"start":353},{"end":526,"start":425},{"end":586,"start":526},{"end":588,"start":586},{"end":619,"start":588},{"end":643,"start":619},{"end":664,"start":643},{"end":720,"start":664},{"end":776,"start":720}],"status":"active","text":"Letter from the pretend river-post club:\r\nOur Foam Barges are also called cloud ferries; these names refer to the same toy.\r\nFor Foam Barges, do not dispatch a parcel if the stamp is missing.\r\nDispatch with a stamp is conditional on the envelope being dry.\r\nP.S. A damp envelope may travel only inside a blue sleeve; this exception qualifies dispatch.\r\nA higher dryness rating means a lower blur tendency, not a higher one.\r\nOne note calls the sleeve blue; a second calls its colour unknown. Do not resolve the disagreement.\r\nThe club-wide bell closes all desks after the final verse.\r\n\r\nAnnex: unrelated counter game\r\nScope: Pebble Counters\r\nAliases: stone tabs\r\nKeep Pebble Counters under the woven cover until noon.\r\nKeep Pebble Counters under the woven cover until noon.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-3981f0e8264100841775e8c781660c754bd8d8437e5a11fe72c209d41ae09edb"},"item-7efae9de56d3e90defc3fd0324c03ddf":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-80de114a93d0fde97e76abf8b484d1dc0a8b1ecbd05a6410cff802b675da26b8"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-7efae9de56d3e90defc3fd0324c03ddf","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":3186,"start":3167},{"end":3187,"start":3186},{"end":3289,"start":3187},{"end":3390,"start":3289},{"end":3410,"start":3390},{"end":3411,"start":3410},{"end":3512,"start":3411},{"end":3607,"start":3512},{"end":3616,"start":3607},{"end":3617,"start":3616}],"status":"active","text":"## Registry scores\n\n`reliability_score` is 10 = highly reliable, 1 = frequent failures. It runs in the opposite direction\nto likelihood. New starters routinely invert it. `criticality_score` runs in the expected direction,\n10 = most critical.\n\nNeither is sufficient on its own. Criticality is a starting point for impact, reliability a starting\npoint for likelihood; the finding text moves both. A reliable item with a crack in it is still\ncracked.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-80de114a93d0fde97e76abf8b484d1dc0a8b1ecbd05a6410cff802b675da26b8"},"item-8724277b28d78ba818a80fdae46e1aaf":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-9cd1a06eec94ab61c09f94806d3e2c07514bbe0da011bba32ba8a6df86e4c5c9"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":["purple bridges"],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Equipment: Plum-Arcs\r\n","unit_id":"u0005"},{"quote":"Aliases: purple bridges\r\n","unit_id":"u0006"}],"item_id":"item-8724277b28d78ba818a80fdae46e1aaf","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Plum-Arcs"],"source_id":"eval_orchard","source_sha256":"412ea94c07b410bb43a46c04e98de2acfcaca0d5641e39f9f6f8e035f893d66c","spans":[{"end":121,"start":96},{"end":143,"start":121},{"end":168,"start":143},{"end":191,"start":168},{"end":242,"start":191},{"end":306,"start":242},{"end":327,"start":306},{"end":390,"start":327},{"end":457,"start":390},{"end":459,"start":457}],"status":"active","text":"## Branch for plum-arcs\r\nEquipment: Plum-Arcs\r\nAliases: purple bridges\r\n- Is the token round?\r\n  - Yes: do not fold Plum-Arcs until the whistle.\r\n  - No: leave the arc undecided; the token shape is not known.\r\n- Exception branch:\r\n  - A square silver token permits folding before the whistle.\r\n  - This exception qualifies the round-token folding restriction.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-9cd1a06eec94ab61c09f94806d3e2c07514bbe0da011bba32ba8a6df86e4c5c9"},"item-89d94479c6f78495658d8a1c8082c4a3":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-7d092d17031e58771702fd76c77bf2e88ddd3a0fb7f1b07859ceab6c00e0d27a"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-89d94479c6f78495658d8a1c8082c4a3","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":1278,"start":1257},{"end":1279,"start":1278},{"end":1378,"start":1279},{"end":1478,"start":1378},{"end":1581,"start":1478},{"end":1677,"start":1581},{"end":1688,"start":1677},{"end":1689,"start":1688},{"end":1790,"start":1689},{"end":1893,"start":1790},{"end":1894,"start":1893}],"status":"active","text":"## What moves impact\n\nUp: absence of redundancy; Safety Critical Elements, which exist because a major accident scenario\ndepends on them and are judged against that scenario rather than against repair cost; failures that\ndegrade a protection layer rather than causing direct loss; delayed or hidden consequences — loss of\ncorrosion inhibitor has no effect today and a substantial effect in eighteen months; escalation\npotential.\n\nDown: redundancy that is available and capable; items that can be bypassed without loss of function;\natmospheric, non-hydrocarbon, low-energy services; consequences limited to housekeeping or appearance.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-7d092d17031e58771702fd76c77bf2e88ddd3a0fb7f1b07859ceab6c00e0d27a"},"item-8f79eb9758c062995e31d11f44f79069":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-42185b59c6f3732373a2b0c52052dc1913b2e10ebe38ea8d0a42122c525eac77"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"# Integrity and Reliability Notes — Bravo Platform\n","unit_id":"u0001"},{"quote":"## The two questions\n","unit_id":"u0006"},{"quote":"## What moves likelihood\n","unit_id":"u0018"},{"quote":"## What moves impact\n","unit_id":"u0028"},{"quote":"## Two recurring errors\n","unit_id":"u0039"},{"quote":"## Urgency\n","unit_id":"u0049"},{"quote":"## Registry scores\n","unit_id":"u0067"},{"quote":"## Output expectations\n","unit_id":"u0077"}],"item_id":"item-8f79eb9758c062995e31d11f44f79069","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":53,"start":0},{"end":54,"start":53},{"end":156,"start":54},{"end":188,"start":156},{"end":189,"start":188}],"status":"active","text":"# Integrity and Reliability Notes — Bravo Platform\n\nHandover notes from the outgoing Integrity Engineer. Unedited. This is the only written record of how\nfindings are currently triaged.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-42185b59c6f3732373a2b0c52052dc1913b2e10ebe38ea8d0a42122c525eac77"},"item-9a7b1ac8564c7e53dfa1fe6bebc14e4d":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-8dc73e241e2fa65eaa9c2ac01a12d411dc9690f96760b5b29e19c949169c6642"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"# Orchard branching game\r\n","unit_id":"u0001"},{"quote":"## Branch for plum-arcs\r\n","unit_id":"u0004"},{"quote":"## Legend\r\n","unit_id":"u0014"},{"quote":"## Branch for Lemon Cubes\r\n","unit_id":"u0018"}],"item_id":"item-9a7b1ac8564c7e53dfa1fe6bebc14e4d","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"eval_orchard","source_sha256":"412ea94c07b410bb43a46c04e98de2acfcaca0d5641e39f9f6f8e035f893d66c","spans":[{"end":26,"start":0},{"end":94,"start":26},{"end":96,"start":94}],"status":"active","text":"# Orchard branching game\r\nThe following branches concern cardboard fruit, not living plants.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-8dc73e241e2fa65eaa9c2ac01a12d411dc9690f96760b5b29e19c949169c6642"},"item-a716a4a9f49df46101a45a8c47f5a164":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-3fe062a4c361f7cb96d0234c5637b023e732a8653517e03f70b9e4d49fcf19a4"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-a716a4a9f49df46101a45a8c47f5a164","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":3640,"start":3617},{"end":3641,"start":3640},{"end":3743,"start":3641},{"end":3836,"start":3743},{"end":3934,"start":3836},{"end":3935,"start":3934},{"end":4004,"start":3935},{"end":4005,"start":4004},{"end":4067,"start":4005},{"end":4169,"start":4067},{"end":4219,"start":4169},{"end":4277,"start":4219},{"end":4326,"start":4277}],"status":"active","text":"## Output expectations\n\nMaintenance planning needs two lines: what is wrong, on what, and why it matters — readable without\nopening the inspection record, and not a restatement of the original finding text. Where the\nassessment is uncertain, that should be stated rather than resolved by picking a mid-range score.\n\nRecurring causes of loss of confidence in a triage output, in order:\n\n1. Confidently incorrect scores on safety critical equipment.\n2. Summaries that omit a detail that changes the decision — a measurement, a repeat occurrence, the\n   fact that the standby was already unavailable.\n3. The same finding scored differently on different days.\n4. Uniform mid-range scores across all findings.\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-3fe062a4c361f7cb96d0234c5637b023e732a8653517e03f70b9e4d49fcf19a4"},"item-afed18293ce961eb704c4475330366ca":{"decision_reason":null,"review":{"reason":"Isolated software selector diagnostic over unchanged raw C0 output. NOT human content approval, NOT engineering approval, NOT qualification. No evaluator expectations were used to correct metadata.","reviewer":"Softwarefixture NOT humanapproval","revision_id":"sha256-029a515f91707edee091751746dcc609bd69d4cf897f41c4b8cab2a2e6d74637"},"review_state":"reviewed","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"# Loom rehearsal log\r\n","unit_id":"u0001"},{"quote":"## 